 one thing about the school system, what would it be? Explain why and how it would work.', 'Write a critical review of an app or service you use. Evaluate its strengths and weaknesses and suggest improvements.', 'Write an article arguing for or against a four-day working week. Support your view with evidence and answer the main objections.', 'Write a formal email to a public body raising a concern about a local issue. Keep the tone polite but firm.', 'Summarize the key findings of an article or study you read recently, and explain why they matter.', 'Write a short story that begins with the sentence: "The message arrived three hours too late."', 'Discuss where the limits of free speech should lie. Weigh competing principles and reach a nuanced conclusion.', 'Choose a common argument you disagree with. Present it fairly, then take it apart point by point.', 'Write a letter to the editor responding to a recent public debate. Use a measured, persuasive register.', 'Analyze a social or technological trend of the last decade: its causes, its consequences and where it may lead.', 'Write a reflective essay about a belief you once held firmly and later changed. What changed your mind?')) as writing_prompts,
  (select count(*) from public.idioms_phrasal_verbs where phrase in ('turn on', 'turn off', 'sit down', 'come back', 'put on', 'wake up', 'pick up', 'check in', 'throw away', 'in a hurry', 'make up your mind', 'keep an eye on', 'run out of', 'set up', 'take after', 'the last straw', 'get cold feet', 'in the long run', 'put up with', 'back up', 'cut down on', 'a drop in the ocean', 'on the fence', 'jump to conclusions', 'phase out', 'rule out', 'a gray area', 'go the extra mile', 'back to square one', 'the tip of the iceberg', 'a Pyrrhic victory', 'a vested interest', 'par for the course', 'muddy the waters', 'hinge on', 'devil''s advocate')) as idioms;
